      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::003"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nanoparticles are initially crystallized as a solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The controlled compositional intervention is variation of Ni content in CoCrCuFeMnNix alloys.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::003"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ni series has Co:Cr:Cu:Fe:Mn:Ni molar ratios of 1:1:1:1:1:x for x = 0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, and 2.0.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::003"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The CoCrCuFeMnNix powders are prepared by mechanical alloying.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::003"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The processing is performed under vacuum conditions.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::003"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant stability range is 473–1923 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Varying Ni content in CoCrCuFeMnNix produces a single FCC solid-solution phase.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::002"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The single FCC solid solution has good thermodynamic stability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::002"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The single FCC solid solution has excellent ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10144805::page::002"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermodynamic stability and ductility of the FCC phase cause structural and chemical stability to be maintained.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Structural and chemical stability is maintained relative to the initial solid-solution baseline throughout 473–1923 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The controlled comparison subjects CoCrCuFeMnNix compositions with different Ni contents to mechanical alloying and annealing.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Phase evolution will be measured by XRD and morphology and composition will be assessed by SEM.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.measurements",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
